{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "domain",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 280,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[凸集|Convex sets]]\n\nEvery segment between every pair of points stays in the set, including every mixture weight from zero to one.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n任取两点、任取0到1之间的权重，混合点都留在集合内。"
    },
    {
      "id": "shape",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 470,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 280,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[凹凸性|Convex and concave functions]]\n\nOn a convex domain, a convex function lies at or below every chord; a concave function lies at or above. Neither definition requires differentiability.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n凸函数不高于输出的加权平均，凹函数不低于它；不要求可导。"
    },
    {
      "id": "level",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 940,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[水平集|Level sets]]\n\nFor a fixed function, domain and value k, collect the allowed inputs with f(x) = k. These are inputs, not points on the graph.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n固定函数、定义域与 k：收集 f(x) = k 的输入，不是图像上的点。"
    },
    {
      "id": "upper",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1410,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[上轮廓集|Upper contour sets]]\n\nWithin the stated domain, collect inputs with f(x) ≥ k. Equality is included. Increasing k cannot enlarge this set.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n定义域内满足 f(x) ≥ k 的输入，含等号；提高门槛不会扩大集合。"
    },
    {
      "id": "lower",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1880,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[下轮廓集|Lower contour sets]]\n\nWithin the stated domain, collect inputs with f(x) ≤ k. Equality is included. Increasing k cannot shrink this set.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n定义域内满足 f(x) ≤ k 的输入，含等号；提高门槛不会缩小集合。"
    },
    {
      "id": "tangent",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 370,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[凹性一阶判据|First-order concavity criterion]]\n\nFor a differentiable function on an open convex domain, concavity is equivalent to every tangent affine approximation being a global upper bound.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n对开凸域上的可微函数，凹性等价于每个切平面都是全域上界。"
    },
    {
      "id": "hessian",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 470,
      "y": 370,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[Hessian凹凸性判据|Hessian concavity criterion]]\n\nFor a $C^2$ function on an open convex domain, concavity is equivalent to a negative-semidefinite Hessian at every point.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\nC² 开凸域上：凹性等价于 Hessian 处处半负定。"
    },
    {
      "id": "implies",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 940,
      "y": 370,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 280,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[凹性推出拟凹性|Concavity and quasiconcavity]]\n\nOn a convex domain, concavity keeps mixture values at least the weighted endpoint average, hence at least the smaller value. The converse fails.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n凹性保住加权平均，因而保住较小端点值；拟凹性推不回凹性。"
    },
    {
      "id": "qc",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1410,
      "y": 370,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 280,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[拟凹函数|Quasiconcave functions]]\n\nA real-valued function on a convex domain is quasiconcave when every upper contour set is convex. No differentiability is required.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n凸域上的实值函数：每个上轮廓集都凸，不要求可导。"
    },
    {
      "id": "qv",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1880,
      "y": 370,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 280,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[拟凸函数|Quasiconvex functions]]\n\nA real-valued function on a convex domain is quasiconvex when every lower contour set is convex. Every real threshold is tested.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n凸域上的实值函数：每个下轮廓集都凸，必须覆盖全部实数门槛。"
    },
    {
      "id": "station",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 740,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[凹函数驻点全局最优|Stationary points and global maxima]]\n\nFor a differentiable concave function on an open convex domain, zero gradient gives a global maximum.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n开凸域上的可微凹函数：零梯度代入切平面上界，得到全局最大。"
    },
    {
      "id": "strict",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 470,
      "y": 740,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[严格凹与负定Hessian|Strict concavity and the Hessian]]\n\nFor $C^2$ functions on an open convex domain, a negative-definite Hessian everywhere is sufficient for strict concavity. The converse fails.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n处处负定足够；严格凹不要求处处负定。"
    },
    {
      "id": "sum",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 940,
      "y": 740,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[凹函数非负加权和|Nonnegative sums of concave functions]]\n\nA finite sum with fixed nonnegative weights preserves concavity on a common convex domain; adding an affine term also preserves it.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n同一凸域上的凹函数，有限个固定非负权重保持凹性；加仿射项也保持凹性。"
    },
    {
      "id": "min",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1410,
      "y": 740,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 280,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[拟凹性线段判据|Minimum-endpoint criterion]]\n\nOn a convex domain, quasiconcavity is equivalent to every mixture value being at least the smaller endpoint value, for every pair and every 0 ≤ t ≤ 1.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n凸域上，任意两点与 0 ≤ t ≤ 1 的混合值不低于较小端点值，等价于拟凹性。"
    },
    {
      "id": "max",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1880,
      "y": 740,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 280,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[拟凸性线段判据|Maximum-endpoint criterion]]\n\nOn a convex domain, quasiconvexity is equivalent to every mixture value being at most the larger endpoint value, for every pair and every 0 ≤ t ≤ 1.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n凸域上，任意两点与 0 ≤ t ≤ 1 的混合值不超过较大端点值，等价于拟凸性。"
    },
    {
      "id": "local",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1110,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[凸优化全局性|Local and global optima]]\n\nOn a convex feasible set, every local maximum of a concave function is global. Differentiability is unnecessary.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n凹目标加凸可行域：局部最大即全局最大，不要求可导。"
    },
    {
      "id": "exist",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 470,
      "y": 1110,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[严格凹不保证解存在|Uniqueness and attainment]]\n\nStrict concavity on a convex feasible set gives at most one maximizer. Nonemptiness and attainment need separate proofs.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n凸可行域上严格凹，只保证最大点至多一个；非空与取得性另证。"
    },
    {
      "id": "mixture",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 940,
      "y": 1110,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[拟凹效用与混合偏好|Quasiconcave utility and mixtures]]\n\nOn a convex consumption domain, each mixture is at least as good as the worse endpoint. Equal endpoint utilities make this a guarantee relative to both.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n凸消费域上，混合至少不差于较差端点；两端效用相等时，便能保证同时不差于两端。"
    },
    {
      "id": "transform",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1410,
      "y": 1110,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[单调变换保持拟凹性|Monotone transformations]]\n\nA real-valued outer function, nondecreasing on all values taken by f, preserves quasiconcavity on the same convex domain. Strict increase also preserves the ranking of f's values.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n实值外函数在 f 的值域上非减，就保留拟凹性；严格递增还保留原值的完整排序。"
    },
    {
      "id": "station-bound",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1880,
      "y": 1110,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 280,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[拟凹驻点不保证最优|Quasiconcavity and stationary points]]\n\nOn the real line, x³ is quasiconcave and has derivative zero at zero, but values of both signs occur arbitrarily close to zero.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n实线上的 x³ 拟凹，零点导数为零，却在任意小邻域都有更大和更小的值。"
    },
    {
      "id": "mono",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1480,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[一维单调函数的拟凹拟凸性|Monotone functions on an interval]]\n\nA nondecreasing or nonincreasing real function on an interval is both quasiconcave and quasiconvex. Continuity is unnecessary.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n区间上的非减或非增函数既拟凹又拟凸，不要求连续。"
    },
    {
      "id": "peak",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 470,
      "y": 1480,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[一维单峰函数拟凹性|Single-peaked functions]]\n\nOn an interval, nondecrease up to c and nonincrease after c imply quasiconcavity. Both restrictions include c; flat tops and jumps are allowed.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n区间上，含 c 的左段非减、右段非增，便拟凹；允许平顶与跳跃。"
    },
    {
      "id": "mrs",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 940,
      "y": 1480,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[边际替代率|Marginal rate of substitution]]\n\nFor C¹ utility with u₂ ≠ 0, a local indifference graph satisfies MRS₁₂ = u₁/u₂ = −dx₂/dx₁. With positive marginal utilities, this is the local amount of good 2 surrendered per unit of good 1.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\nC¹ 效用且 u₂≠0 时，沿局部无差异图像有 MRS₁₂=u₁/u₂=−dx₂/dx₁；正边际效用时，表示局部少多少商品2换商品1。"
    },
    {
      "id": "mrs-shape",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1410,
      "y": 1480,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[拟凹效用的递减MRS|Diminishing MRS]]\n\nOn the stated regular graph of one utility level, positive marginal utilities and a convex upper region make MRS nonincreasing as good 1 rises. Constancy is allowed.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n同一效用水平的正规图像上，正边际效用与凸上轮廓区域使 MRS 非增，允许不变。"
    },
    {
      "id": "mono-bound",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1770,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 280,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[多元单调不推拟凹|Coordinatewise increase]]\n\nOn the positive quadrant, x² + y² increases in each coordinate. Yet (2,1) and (1,2) give 5, while their midpoint gives 9/2: quasiconcavity fails.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n正象限上逐坐标递增仍不足：(2,1)、(1,2) 都取5，中点仅取9/2。"
    },
    {
      "id": "peak-bound",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 470,
      "y": 1770,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 280,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[唯一峰值不推拟凹|A unique peak]]\n\nA unique global maximum controls only the highest value. The negative-square-root example has that maximum but a nonconvex upper region at level −1.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n唯一全局最大点不控制全部低门槛；负平方根例在 −1 水平的上轮廓集不凸。"
    },
    {
      "id": "utility",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1410,
      "y": 1880,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[效用函数|Utility functions]]\n\nA utility score represents the ranking of specified consumption bundles. Higher scores mean preferred bundles; equal scores mean indifference.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n效用分数表示确定商品束的偏好排序：高分更好，同分一样好。"
    },
    {
      "id": "indifference",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 940,
      "y": 1880,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[无差异曲线|Indifference curves]]\n\nCollect the allowed two-good bundles with the same utility. This is an input level set; smoothness and a downward slope need further assumptions.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n收集效用相等的二商品组合；这是输入水平集，光滑或向下倾斜另需条件。"
    }
  ],
